\begin{align*}
x^y+1&=y^x,\\
2x^y&=y^x+7.
\end{align*}

query_en:
Determine the ordered pair of positive integers $(x, y)$ that satisfy the following system of equations:

\begin{align*}
x^y + 1 &= y^x,\\
2x^y &= y^x + 7.
\end{align*}

response_en:
The probability of no snow on each of the next three days is $\left(\frac{1}{3}\right)^3=\frac{1}{27}$.
Therefore, the probability of having at least one day with snow is $1-\frac{1}{27}=\boxed{\frac{26}{27}}$.
The answer is: \frac{26}{27}

